WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.260
Search Cameron County property records from your terminal.

00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:09.160
This is Texas scraper kit version 1.0.1 installed from the release package.

00:00:10.250 --> 00:00:12.290
Enter the county and the owner name here.

00:00:12.950 --> 00:00:14.650
We're searching for space exploration,

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:17.570
limiting the export to three records

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:19.550
and saving the results to a file.

00:00:20.170 --> 00:00:22.390
The command queries the live appraisal source.

00:00:23.458 --> 00:00:25.698
open that file and inspect what came back,

00:00:25.878 --> 00:00:29.478
parcel numbers, listed owners, street addresses and market values.

00:00:30.378 --> 00:00:33.598
These are appraisal records. The values shown are not purchase prices

00:00:33.598 --> 00:00:35.778
and a broad search still needs review.

00:00:36.917 --> 00:00:41.137
take the first parcel number and run an exact account look-up. Now we're

00:00:41.137 --> 00:00:45.897
checking one specific record with its legal description, tax year and a link

00:00:45.897 --> 00:00:47.697
back to the county's property page.

00:00:48.667 --> 00:00:51.027
follow that link to the official Cameron Portal.

00:00:51.867 --> 00:00:54.467
Compare the parcel number and owner against the export

00:00:55.187 --> 00:00:57.527
for a purchase history continue to recorded deeds.

00:00:58.187 --> 00:00:59.967
Appraisal data alone doesn't establish

00:00:59.967 --> 00:01:00.947
when a sale happened.

00:01:01.958 --> 00:01:07.138
That's the workflow, query, real public records, export the data and follow the source, get

00:01:07.138 --> 00:01:11.938
the commands, the full walkthrough and a free business lookup sampler from the linked tutorial.
